TOML 1.1 allows inline tables to span multiple lines: newlines (and comments) are permitted between the braces and between key/value pairs, and a trailing comma after the last pair is allowed, for example `x = {
  a = 1,
  b = 2,
}`. Empty inline tables written over several lines must also parse. Add support for this in tomli's parser. The TOML-test suite cases for this feature are currently listed in tests/test_data.py as expected to fail; make them pass, remove them from that list, and add test data.
